    "title": "Actor Max Greenfield, of 'New Girl' fame, to visit Northern Michigan University - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Alexandria Bournonville ,\n15 hours ago\nMARQUETTE, Mich. (WBUP/WJMN) — Max Greenfield, widely known for his roles on \"New Girl\" and \"The Neighborhood,\" will be visiting Northern Michigan University at 7 p.m. Tuesday, April 7.\nGreenfield is an Emmy- and Golden Globe-nominated actor best known for his iconic role as Schmidt in the hit comedy series \"New Girl.\" He also currently starts as Dave Johnson in the sitcom \"The Neighborhood\" and is expected to appear in season four of \"The White Lotus,\" according to NMU's Northern Today .\nThe actor is brought to Marquette by the NMU student organization Platform Personalities. At the event in the Northern Center, attendees will have the opportunity to listen to Greenfield, interact with him, and ask questions.\nGeneral admission tickets to the event are available free for NMU students (one per ID) and will go on sale to the general public for $5 on Friday, March 27. They can be purchased at tickets.nmu.edu .\nCOPYRIGHT 2026 BY MY UP NOW – WBUP/WJMN. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. THIS MATERIAL MAY NOT BE PUBLISHED, BROADCAST, REWRITTEN OR REDISTRIBUTED",
    "summary": "MARQUETTE, Mich. (WBUP/WJMN) — Max Greenfield, widely known for his roles on \"New Girl\" and \"The Neighborhood,\" will be visiting Northern Michigan University at 7 p.m. Tuesday, April 7. Greenfield is an Emmy- and Golden Globe-nominated actor best known for his iconic role as Schmidt in the hit comedy series \"New Girl.\" He also currently starts as Dave Johnson in the sitcom \"The Neighborhood\" and is expected to appear in season four of \"The White Lotus,\" according to NMU's Northern Today . The actor is brought to Marquette by the NMU student organization Platform Personalities.",
